// A full-notation tab whose first bar beams UP (a bass run on the low strings): the tempo
// mark must clear the beam, as it clears the same beam on the notation staff and as
// LilyPond's MetronomeMark clears it on a TabStaff (\tabFullNotation reverts the Stem and
// Beam stencils, and the axis group's skyline carries every member — measured 2.26.0,
// session 321, owner report on the Billie Jean bassTab book). Until 2026-09-02 the tab's
// skyline held only its fret digits, so the tempo's quiet baseline ran through the beam.
octave absolute
tempo 117
key d major
time 4/4

part bl {
  clef bass
  tuning bass
  section A { fis,,8\4 cis,\3 e,\3 fis,\3 e,\3 cis,\3 b,,\4 cis,\3 | fis,,8\4 cis,\3 e,\3 fis,\3 e,\3 cis,\3 b,,\4 cis,\3 | }
}

form main { A }

score main "tab-tempo-over-beam" {
  tab bl as full
}
